  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Seraj Ahmad vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of ... on 19 September, 2024 Author: Rajesh Singh Chauhan Bench: Rajesh Singh Chauhan High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:65137 Court No. - 4 Case :- Writ - A No. - 6709 of 2024 Petitioner :- Seraj Ahmad Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of Food Safety And Drugs Administra Counsel for Petitioner :- Syed Aftab Ahmad,Asma Shamim,Meghna Singhal,Mohammed Hamza Sha Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Rajesh Singh Chauhan,J. Heard. This Court has passed order dated 21.8.2024 which reads as under : \"Heard Sri Syed Aftab Ahmad, learned counsel for the petitioner and Sri Narendra Kumar Pandey, learned Standing Counsel.",
    "facts": "By means of the present petitioner, the petitioner has assailed the suspension order dated 30.07.2024.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the petitioner has stated that the impugned suspension order has been passed in violation of the Rule IV of the The U.P. Government Servant (Discipline and Appeal) Seraj Ahmad vs State Of U.P. Thru. Prin. Secy. Deptt. Of ... on 19 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/144951176/ 1 Rules, 1999, in as much as, the petitioner has been suspended on frivolous grounds. He has further submitted that though the suspension order does not qualify the test of Rule 4 of the Rules, 1999 but the petitioner may submit his defence reply to the charge-sheet and shall cooperate in the departmental proceedings but any protection may be given to the petitioner considering the fact that the petitioner is going to retire on 30.10.2024."
  },
